 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "vax upright brush thingy stopped spinnin, sucks ok thru the hose but nt pickin up off carpet. smelt like burnin rubber b4 it stopped"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nA burning or hot-plastic smell, smoke, scorching or melting can mean an electrical fault or a fire risk. Stop using it, switch it off and unplug it (or turn it off at the fuse box), and don't run it again — not even as a test — until it has been checked by a qualified engineer. Given the burning rubber smell and the brush stopping, it is safest to stop using the vacuum until a qualified engineer has checked it. The most likely causes are hair jamming the roller or a snapped drive belt, which can cause friction and heat. Please switch off and unplug the machine first. Then turn the floorhead over and try spinning the brush bar by hand to see if it is tangled or free."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok unplugged it and turned it over. brushbar turns by hand but its tight, theres loads of hair n a tassel wrapped round the ends"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nBecause the brush bar is still tight even after you’ve cleared some debris, it suggests there may be more hair or thread wrapped around the ends of the roller that are harder to see. You might need a pair of scissors or a seam ripper to carefully cut away the tangled material at the end caps without damaging the brush bar. Once you’ve done this, let me know if it spins freely by hand.\n[Panel: \"To check a suitable replacement — Enter your model number below. Once we have the model I can check whether a suitable replacement is available. It's usually on a sticker inside the door or around the frame, or on the back of the appliance.\"]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "cut the hair n tassel off and it spins free by hand now. model on the back sticker says U85-AS-Be if u need it"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nThat’s excellent news! It sounds like the hair jam was indeed causing the tightness and likely the burning smell from the friction. To help prevent this from happening again, I’d recommend checking the brush bar for tangles every few weeks, especially if you have pets or long-haired family members. Is there anything else I can assist you with today?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "its still not spinnin tho, shud i look at the belt? i can take the sole plate off"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nYes, please check the drive belt next since the brush spins freely by hand but isn't turning when powered. Unplug the vacuum first, then remove the sole plate to see if the rubber belt is still on its pulleys or has snapped and stretched. It's a common cause for this symptom after clearing a jam."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok took the sole plate off. belt is snapped, 2 bits, one bit has a shiny melted looking edge. no idea what part number it is tho"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nThat snapped belt with melted edges explains why the brush stopped spinning and caused that burning smell. The good news is this is a very common issue on Vax uprights like yours, and replacing the drive belt is usually straightforward. You can find a compatible replacement belt by searching for \"Vax U85-AS-BE drive belt\" online or at most DIY stores. Once you fit it back in place with the sole plate, your brush bar should spin normally again."
  }
 ],
